WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.318
Targeting answers two questions: which merchandise
qualifies, and which shopper may receive the offer?

2
00:00:06.318 --> 00:00:13.539
Our example uses Coral as the trigger and a
twenty-percent Sun reward. In Conditions, select the

3
00:00:13.539 --> 00:00:20.760
product; in Rewards, choose the separate target. This
demo selects whole products. When a product has

4
00:00:20.760 --> 00:00:27.078
multiple variants, expand the picker for exact SKU
choices. Whole-product scope can include future

5
00:00:27.078 --> 00:00:32.042
variants, while an exact-variant selection remains
restricted to its configured IDs.

6
00:00:33.092 --> 00:00:39.606
Open Audience Targeting in Review and launch. Add the
synthetic customer tag education-vip. This only

7
00:00:39.606 --> 00:00:47.423
configures a filter; it does not create a customer or
assign that tag to anyone. Tagged customer eligibility

8
00:00:47.423 --> 00:00:52.635
requires the relevant signed-in customer context.
Product tags classify merchandise; customer tags

9
00:00:52.635 --> 00:00:59.583
restrict shoppers. An empty audience filter means
everyone, not nobody, so review it before saving a

10
00:00:59.583 --> 00:01:00.452
public offer.

11
00:01:01.502 --> 00:01:07.459
Keep Include selected countries and select United
States. That is different from excluding the United

12
00:01:07.459 --> 00:01:13.416
States and allowing other countries. The example now
requires both the intended merchandise and this

13
00:01:13.416 --> 00:01:20.565
audience context. A shopper using U.S. dollars is not
proof that they are browsing from the United States.

14
00:01:20.565 --> 00:01:26.125
Currency thresholds, country filters and a final
delivery address are distinct checks; do not

15
00:01:26.125 --> 00:01:27.713
substitute one for another.

16
00:01:28.763 --> 00:01:35.927
Save inactive and reopen the audience section. Confirm
education-vip, United States and Include mode, as well

17
00:01:35.927 --> 00:01:43.539
as the trigger and reward selections. This video
verifies the stored filter, not a real customer login

18
00:01:43.539 --> 00:01:50.256
or delivery change. Before launch, test a matching
customer, a nonmatching customer and a signed-out

19
00:01:50.256 --> 00:01:57.420
session, plus allowed and excluded countries. Recheck
after a market switch and compare the final checkout.

20
00:01:57.420 --> 00:02:01.002
Keep public messages consistent with all these
restrictions.
